WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.270
Takagi Sakuya
Maruo Eiichiro

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.540
<i>If we're neck-and-neck 
and I take the first set,</i>

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.270
<i>I'll immediately have the upper hand.</i>

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:11.280
<i>I need this set in order to 
corner him in the second set.</i>

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.950
<i>I have to break somehow!</i>

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.230
<i>After I defeated Nabae that day, 
I undoubtedly moved forward.</i>

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.640
<i>In order to move ahead even more,</i>

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.960
<i>I'll beat Nabae in this tournament, too!</i>

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.610
<i>I'm different from you.</i>

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.420
<i>You don't know how miserable 
it feels not to be able to win!</i>

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.940
<i>That's why I'll do whatever it takes!</i>

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.510
<i>Good serve!</i>

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.850
<i>A drop shot here?!</i>

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.560
<i>He can go for the left, right, or above...</i>

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.110
<i>Or maybe he'll hit it low this time?</i>

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.610
<i>Right at me?!</i>

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.870
<i>Why did he go for such a risky shot?!</i>

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.120
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.630
Good, Evil, and Rules

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.150
5-3. Maruo.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.610
He was totally going for his face just now!

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.130
He's shown no sportsmanship, 
and he has a horrible attitude.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.210
He should at least apologize.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:07.180
Well, it's a tournament, after all. 
I'm sure it's fine.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.130
Maruo, get him back!

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.210
<i>He was watching that one closely.</i>

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.590
<i>That was close.</i>

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.660
<i>He could've won the point by hitting to the side,</i>

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:22.740
<i>but he chose to try to hit me with 
the ball and shake me up mentally.</i>

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.550
<i>Yet he isn't even trying to 
hide his malicious intent.</i>

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.710
<i>You've gotta be kidding me.</i>

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.690
<i>There's no way I can lose 
to a dirty player like him!</i>

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:43.710
<i>I've been trying to calm down, 
but I'm not getting the results I want.</i>

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:47.820
<i>Is there some way I can deflect this 
frustration toward the match, then?</i>

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:53.060
<i>My match with Ide-kun went well because 
I confronted the pressure head-on.</i>

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.620
<i>Then maybe even anger</i>

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.460
<i>can be turned into a strength 
if I get it out of my system.</i>

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.930
<i>All right!</i>

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.230
<i>I'm leading by two points,</i>

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.430
<i>so I can go for it.</i>

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:07.430
<i>Slam all the frustration I've been holding in</i>

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.560
<i>into the ball!</i>

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:12.450
Out.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:13.750
5-4. Maruo.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.400
Hey, is he okay?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.080
Maybe that last move rattled him?

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.280
Bro is good-natured, 
but even he's getting mad.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.430
<i>My delivery was good, but my aim was bad.</i>

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.700
<i>But if I adjust it, it should work.</i>

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.290
<i>If I can get my anger out, 
I'll kill two birds with one stone!</i>

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.790
<i>I'll unleash my rage!</i>

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:43.630
<i>Crap! I swung too soon, 
and it hit the frame!</i>

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.170
<i>But my swing itself has power to it.</i>

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.510
<i>If I can just match up the timing...</i>

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.210
<i>Did I put too much spin on it?!</i>

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.440
<i>Match up to the faster swing...</i>

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:01.440
Out. 5-all.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.230
<i>I'm getting enough power,</i>

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:08.790
<i>but I can't get the timing right.</i>

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.290
<i>I just need to get it in, 
but this is killing my accuracy.</i>

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.970
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.420
<i>Anger can't be advantageous in a match.</i>

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.570
<i>Only two and a half years behind him...</i>

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:21.380
<i>Where he lacks experience, 
he </i>really<i> lacks experience.</i>

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:26.140
<i>My heart rate is increasing, and my 
mind isn't as clear as it usually is.</i>

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:30.390
<i>I didn't think it would affect 
subsequent points, too.</i>

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.180
<i>I have to take some time with this one.</i>

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.690
Excuse me. Please call a time violation.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.380
Fifteen seconds.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:42.970
Huh?!

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:48.320
Maruo, you seem to be taking more
time between points. Please be mindful.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.200
Uh, right! Sorry!

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:54.950
From this point on, if you exceed twenty 
seconds, you'll receive a warning.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.600
<i>He really is a nasty person!</i>

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.500
<i>No, no, getting angry only makes things worse!</i>

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.170
<i>I have to switch gears!</i>

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.960
<i>I have to absolve my rage somehow.</i>

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:14.370
<i>That's right. Takagi-kun is 
still playing within the rules.</i>

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:19.190
<i>Which means I just wasn't 
considering the methods</i>

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.400
<i>that Takagi-kun chose in order to win.</i>

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.170
<i>After all,</i>

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.820
<i>if I'm the one who hit a shot
he could aim back at my face,</i>

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.200
<i>then I'm the one who failed to be ready for it.</i>

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.010
<i>And my own inexperience is why 
I was distracted by his stomping.</i>

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.840
<i>And an underhand serve is a legitimate tactic.</i>

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:41.580
Fifteen seconds.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.940
<i>Five more seconds and I'll get a warning.</i>

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:48.500
<i>But breaking a 5-all tie is the 
most important point in the game.</i>

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.860
Takagi     Maruo

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.950
<i>Whoever scores next will have set point.</i>

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.130
<i>I can't miss that, no matter what!</i>

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:59.250
Maruo, twenty seconds have 
passed. This is a warning.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:03.210
Whoa, Maruo got a warning.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:06.110
If he waits another twenty seconds 
and gets another warning,

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.900
he'll lose a point, right?

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:10.420
What are you doing, Bro?

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.080
<i>I'll accept the warning.</i>

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:22.650
<i>Right now, it's more crucial 
that I win this point.</i>

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:27.940
<i>To do that, I'll use the remaining 
twenty seconds to calm my agitation.</i>

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:33.520
<i>Intentionally accepting a warning... 
I guess I'm not so different from Takagi-kun.</i>

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.390
<i>I'm in no position to judge him.</i>

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:40.600
<i>It's the rules that decide 
good and evil on the court.</i>

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.610
<i>Takagi-kun is just playing with his own style.</i>

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.130
<i>I just have to play with my own style, too!</i>

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:03.740
<i>All right...</i>

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.760
<i>I'm not angry anymore!</i>

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.350
<i>What's with that face?</i>

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.010
<i>If you think you can do it, just try!</i>

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.450
<i>Getting angry won't make anything better.</i>

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:23.980
<i>I'll just have to believe that 
my body understands that, too.</i>

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:28.980
<i>A serve and dash!</i>

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:31.110
<i>Off the frame!</i>

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.110
6-5. Maruo.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.120
<i>Th-That was close!</i>

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.930
<i>But even if my body was stiff, 
I was able to win that point</i>

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.120
<i>because I went for it without being timid.</i>

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:46.040
<i>And if I think about it rationally,</i>

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.820
<i>what's scary about Takagi-kun 
isn't his lack of etiquette.</i>

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:51.620
<i>It's the way his movements 
haven't weakened at all,</i>

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.560
<i>his stamina, that's the real threat.</i>

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:59.450
<i>If I lose this first set, I'll have 
to face that stamina in a full set.</i>

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.960
<i>For me to realize this now...</i>

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.380
<i>I lost sight of what was truly important.</i>

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:08.590
<i>Huh?</i>

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:12.530
<i>Now that my anger's subsided, 
I suddenly feel pressure.</i>

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:19.450
<i>But if I can control this pressure, 
I can use it to my advantage.</i>

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.660
<i>All right. Set point.</i>

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.000
<i>I'll finish it here.</i>

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.640
<i>He's holding out better than I expected.</i>

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:30.920
<i>But now that I've come this far,
all that's left is to crush him head-on.</i>

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.470
<i>I don't know what Nabae sees in this guy,</i>

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.970
<i>but I refuse to accept it!</i>

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:45.220
<i>After a powerful, flat return, 
I'll go for a shot I haven't used yet!</i>

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:46.850
<i>A drop shot!</i>

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:57.860
First set winner: Maruo. Score: 7-6.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.360
Yes!

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:05.370
<i>That was a good serve, so why?!</i>

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.870
Takagi Sakuya
Maruo Eiichiro

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:14.880
<i>With my anger gone, maybe I can 
actually afford to feel pressure now.</i>

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:20.890
Rage

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:20.890
Heavy pressure

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:20.890
<i>This same feeling of pressure weighing down on 
me that I felt during my match with Ide-kun...</i>

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:22.890
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:24.150
Time.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:32.150
<i>I'll take more risks from the second set onward,</i>

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.150
<i>and kick it up one gear!</i>

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.650
<i>After gaining the upper hand 
with a quick, flat serve,</i>

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.680
<i>go for a deep spin with a light bounce.</i>

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.930
<i>Then a fast slice that's shallow and 
sharp, and doesn't bounce much!</i>

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.480
15-love.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:53.020
<i>What was that?!</i>

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.420
<i>Weren't you getting desperate?!</i>

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.910
<i>This is it!</i>

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:00.130
<i>I lost to Takagi pretty quickly.</i>

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.960
<i>You've gotten so much stronger, Bro.</i>

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:09.690
<i>For Bro, fancy plays like that
are the fruits of his labor.</i>

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.190
Ten sprints!

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:15.190
<i>Bro's practiced all of his 
techniques with perfect balance.</i>

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.190
<i>That's why he can do all sorts of things.</i>

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.730
Okay, that one was good.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.200
Do it like that ten more times!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.860
Next is the backhand!

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.450
<i>That reminds me...</i>

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:33.460
Maruo, have you ever hit a shot 
between your legs before?

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:36.140
That acrobatic move that's for show?

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:40.560
No, it's actually a shot that 
makes sense in certain situations.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.190
If a ball goes overhead, like a lob, 
and you can reach it in time,

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:47.470
but you don't have enough time to 
turn around and hit it properly...

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:51.120
Hitting it between your legs instead 
of forcing yourself to turn around

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.970
gives you more power and makes 
the ball's course harder to predict.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:58.490
That's about how much speed you should have.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:00.510
Th-That was good.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:03.630
He is a former pro, after all.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:04.610
Here, Maruo.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:08.120
<i>Scary!</i>

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:12.630
Go for the ball right before the second bounce.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:15.880
So close!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.220
<i>Take this!</i>

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:19.880
That's it!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.870
That one was good, Maruo.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:22.880
Okay!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:26.890
<i>Bro's growth really is the 
result of all his training.</i>

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.090
Game: Maruo. 1-0.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:30.270
Second set.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.980
<i>All right! I held!</i>

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.270
<i>I'm less stiff, too!</i>

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.220
<i>Weren't you pissed just a moment ago?!</i>

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:42.090
<i>He changed after the first set ended.</i>

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.300
<i>What's going on?!</i>

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.280
<i>I can't find any weaknesses in Takagi-kun,</i>

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:49.020
<i>but I also don't see any strengths 
on the level of Ide-kun or Araya-kun.</i>

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.290
<i>If I can just play my own 
style of tennis, I won't lose!</i>

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:55.140
<i>But I don't know what he'll do next,</i>

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.790
<i>so I have to keep my guard up.</i>

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.300
<i>Damn! I can't predict what he'll do!</i>

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:12.560
<i>I can't lose before I get to play Nabae!</i>

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:15.560
Out.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.590
W-Wasn't that one in?

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:26.320
<i>The ref's judgment is getting worse?</i>

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:31.080
<i>It was on the line, but the ref's 
judgment can't be overturned.</i>

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.540
Game: Maruo. 2-0.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.770
Second set.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:36.940
<i>Damn!</i>

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:48.470
<i>I can't help how much he reminds me of Nabae.</i>

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.290
<i>I broke serve in the second set!</i>

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:54.000
<i>Time to kick it up another gear!</i>

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.690
Takagi Sakuya
Maruo Eiichiro

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.950
<i>I don't know what he's analyzing or how,</i>

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.950
<i>but he's adapting to everything I do instantly!</i>

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.080
<i>What's after that quick flat?</i>

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.590
<i>Will it slide? Bounce?</i>

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.960
<i>Will it be fast? Or slow?</i>

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:25.280
<i>Consecutive quick flat shots!</i>

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.910
Game: Maruo. 3-0.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.450
Second set.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.930
Yes!

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:31.930
<i>Damn!</i>

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:35.960
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.480
If you depend on tricks,

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.940
your tennis will never improve.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.440
<i>It's exactly as Nabae said.</i>

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.340
Game: Maruo. 4-1.

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:49.590
Second set.

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:51.050
<i>I get it already.</i>

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:52.950
<i>This kid...</i>

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.970
Game: Maruo. 5-2.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.130
Second set.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.210
<i>...can't be beaten with tricks!</i>

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.960
Yes! Bro's got match point!

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.880
Game, set, and match. Winner: Maruo.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.660
Score: 7-6, 6-2.

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:13.720
Thank you very much.

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:25.160
<i>But I practiced more than Nabae.</i>

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:28.850
<i>True, I spent a lot of time on
tricky shots and strategies,</i>

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:31.400
<i>but I didn't take fundamental training lightly.</i>

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:33.900
<i>What else am I supposed to do?!</i>

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:36.840
I heard Maruo won again.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.790
An unseeded player made the top four?

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:42.620
Seriously? He started tennis 
in high school, right?

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.590
<i>Wait, so it's just been a bit over
two years since he started?!</i>

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.980
Congratulations, Bro!

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:50.500
Th-Thanks.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:52.250
As expected of you, Bro.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.650
You managed to hang in there.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:55.350
Yeah...

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:59.220
I would've been in trouble 
if he had won the first set.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:02.650
You'll face players like that from time to time,

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:05.860
but you'll never get to the top if you 
always struggle with their antics.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:10.860
Especially if you're planning to play overseas.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.540
R-Right.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.430
The one thing we can say for certain

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:17.800
is that nothing good comes out 
of getting irritated in a match.

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:20.620
Yes, I realized that very clearly.

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:24.060
Being unable to get the
timing right was exhausting,

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:27.630
and I didn't even notice 
the pressure I was under.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:31.850
Pressure comes from the desire to win,

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:35.260
but anger comes from somewhere else.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.180
{A: E... to...}Um...

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:48.050
I see.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:51.810
That's why I do better when I feel pressure.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.880
Right. Pretty surprising, isn't it?

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:02.610
If you were to put all the mental states 
in order, it would look like this.

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:04.290
You'll want to remember this.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:11.000
Pressure comes from wanting to win.
Anger has no ties with wanting to win.
Apathy -> Anger -> Pressure -> Challenge

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:08.010
This will help you determine what route to take

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:11.000
depending on what mental state you're in.

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:17.510
Well, I think this turned into 
a good experience for you.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.450
Uh, hey...

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.510
Do you have a second?

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.520
T-Takagi-kun?

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.950
Is it true that you started tennis in high school?

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:27.770
Huh?

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.850
Um, yeah, that's right.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:34.280
<i>What brought this on?</i>

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:36.840
I-If it's all right with you,

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:40.290
could you tell me what kind 
of training you normally do?

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.550
What kind? Well...

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.940
Are those the notes you were 
taking during the match?

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:52.300
Y-Yeah.

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:54.560
Can I take a look?

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:56.380
Sure.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.060
<i>Wow...</i>

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.060
<i>He took notes on almost every point.</i>

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:11.690
Just remember, doing exactly what he 
does won't necessarily help you improve.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:18.200
You both have different 
personalities and physiques.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:25.470
Maruo's training is specifically 
formulated for him,

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:28.280
whether it's nurturing his 
perfectionist nature

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:31.100
or reinforcing what he
lacks in physical strength.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:35.210
By doing that, he's searching 
for his own style of tennis.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:37.720
<i>His own style of tennis...</i>

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:42.100
<i>I've based my training on 
competing with Nabae.</i>

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.360
It may be none of my business,

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:47.410
but I'm sure there's a 
training style suited for you.

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:54.510
Even today, we would've had a harder time 
if you'd utilized the stamina you're gifted with.

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:55.990
Oh... Right.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.240
Thanks for this.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.990
Oh, no problem.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:04.240
Um, can I ask you something, too?

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.820
Huh? Sure.

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:10.200
I heard that you beat Nabae-kun before.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.710
How did you do it?

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:14.710
Where did you hear that?

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:18.330
You can't even call that a win.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:23.970
We played one-set matches over and over, 
for over nine hours, until I won a single set.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:27.930
<i>Which is why I wanted to 
beat him in an official match.</i>

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:32.050
<i>He played until he won? 
He really is incredible.</i>

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:36.940
<i>And Nabae-kun, who only let
someone this persistent win one set...</i>

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:44.080
Sorry for all that stuff I did during the match.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.390
It's okay. I should apologize, too.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:48.340
See ya.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:49.930
Oh, yeah.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.750
Since you beat me, you better beat Nabae.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.640
Beat who, now?

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.500
Oh, Nabae-kun.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:02.300
I guess that means you won, Maruo-kun.

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:03.800
Yeah.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.090
Then I'll be looking forward to tomorrow.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.810
Me, too.

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.880
<i>Nabae-kun won, too.</i>

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:22.840
<i>So my next opponent is the All-Japan Junior's 
number one player, Nabae-kun.</i>

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:26.320
Maruo-kun was strong, wasn't he?

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:27.330
I guess.

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:30.330
I can't believe he only has two 
and a half years' experience.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.870
Wow, really?

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.760
You didn't know?

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:37.340
I did think he had improved pretty quickly.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:42.360
When I think about it that way, I feel 
like a lot of my effort was meaningless.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.340
There's no such thing as meaningless effort.

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:46.840
Huh?

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:52.180
Today just wasn't your day. 
Your efforts will prevail one day.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.980
Regardless, I'm gonna stop depending 
on sly tricks from now on!

00:20:57.230 --> 00:21:00.110
Huh? You're gonna stop that?

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.200
You're the one who suggested I stop!

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:09.620
Well, that's true, but if you do those 
things wisely, they can be useful.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:12.700
A part of me wants to master 
that kind of thing, too.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:16.440
Then which is it? Not that it matters...

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:19.710
The point is, just doing that alone isn't enough.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:25.480
But at any rate, your desire to win is unmatched.

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:29.390
So you'll continue getting better, 
whether it happens slowly or quickly.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:35.090
Wh-What's with you all of a sudden? 
You're creeping me out.

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:37.900
What? I'm complimenting you.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:42.400
Oh, by the way, there's something 
I wanted to ask you about Maruo-kun.

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:46.740
You really are a scary guy.

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:52.110
Well, Bro, we're finally down to the top four.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:53.450
Y-Yeah...

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:58.170
You even beat Takagi. 
Your skill is definitely the real deal.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:00.690
Fukazawa Yukichi    Takagi Sakuya    Maruo Eiichiro

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.270
I'll be looking forward to 
your match against Nabae!

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:04.050
Nabae Yu

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.280
Maruo Eiichiro

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:15.060
Nabae Yu

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:17.680
<i>I was thoroughly defeated last year.</i>

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:20.660
<i>I've done everything I can since then, and now,</i>

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:22.070
<i>I've finally come this far.</i>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:03.540
Takuma-san, I made it into the top four!

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:06.540
And you're playing Nabae 
tomorrow? That'll be tough.

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:10.480
Nabae-kun doesn't have any physical 
or psychological weaknesses.

00:24:10.480 --> 00:24:12.380
I have no idea how to strategize.

00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:14.610
Oh? You didn't know?

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:18.810
When he was younger, 
he had a huge weakness.

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:21.040
What?! Nabae-kun did?

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:22.830
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Existence is the Driving Force

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:25.020
"Existence is the Driving Force."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
